        "date": "2026-11-08T22:26:50Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(mcp): render_stock - the simulated stock as a PNG image block\n\nA headless agent can now see what the program leaves. render_stock runs\nthe column verdict's program sim (simulate_document, the post gate's\nown), paints its sheet by deviation class, skirts open edges down to\nthe stock floor, and rasterises it on the CPU (new app::raster: edge\nfunctions, z-buffer, flat Lambert, fixed iso/top orthographic camera\nfitted to the scene) into a PNG. Optional toolpath overlay (feed blue,\nplunge amber, rapid red). The answer carries a JSON summary (rest and\ngouge cells/volume/max/where, rest top bounds, stock bounds) and an MCP\nimage content block; tool_ok lifts the reserved _png_base64 key out of\nthe JSON into that block.\n\nDeterministic: single-threaded, scene-fitted camera; pinned by the new\nmcp_render suite (same bytes twice and across sessions, decoded size,\nstock pixels, named refusals for no sim and bad arguments).\n\npng 0.18 (already in Cargo.lock via image) is now a direct dependency of\ncamcraft-app; base64 is a small in-tree RFC 4648 encoder.\n\nFixes #182\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
