      "message": "test(mcp): render_stock pinned on a real cut and a through-cut\n\nrender_stock_shows_what_the_program_cut faces the block 2 mm off the\ntop (stock top 18, rest 40 x 40 x 3 = 4800 mm^3, rest top at 18) and then\ndown to the part top (rest gone, stock top 15): the picture's bytes\nchange, the amber rest region over the part repaints clean, and the\nsummary follows each cut.\n\nrender_stock_refuses_when_no_material_stands faces below the stock\nfloor. The column grid is semi-infinite, so that used to draw a sheet\nhanging under the block; the render now clips the sheet to the stock's\nfloor (columns at or below it are air, walls stop there), which makes\nthe \"no surface to render\" refusal reachable and pinned.\n\nRefs #182\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
